Package: trojka
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: terminal match-three falling blocks game
 Trojka is a curses falling-blocks puzzle game written by Maarten Los in
 1992.  Blocks drop into a well and are cleared when three or more matching
 patterns line up horizontally or diagonally.  Three consecutive collapses
 in a row score a "Trojka" bonus.  Ten difficulty levels are selectable at
 the start of each game.
 .
 This package contains the terminal (ncurses) version, modernised from the
 original K&R C sources to build cleanly on current Linux systems.  High
 scores are kept per user in $HOME/.trojka.scores, so no system-wide score
 file or setgid binary is needed.
